From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:02:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 171/342] network: multicasts and broadcasts do not go to the
 gateway

A multicast to a group without a route of its own (224.0.0.251 for
multicast DNS, say) takes the default route, and send_routed_data()
put the gateway's address in the buffer's destination. ARP then made
the Ethernet multicast address from the gateway's IPv4 address
(01:00:5e:2a:00:01 for 10.42.0.1 instead of 01:00:5e:00:00:fb), and
only hosts whose interface takes every frame saw the packet: a music
player's queries for shared music libraries reached one server and not another.
Broadcasts and multicasts now keep their destination address.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/add-ons/kernel/network/stack/datalink.cpp | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/network/stack/datalink.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/network/stack/datalink.cpp
index df4fae254c..2d9b7ad2dc 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/network/stack/datalink.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/network/stack/datalink.cpp
@@ -400,11 +400,16 @@ datalink_send_routed_data(struct net_route* route, net_buffer* buffer)
 		return status;
 	}
 
-	if ((route->flags & RTF_GATEWAY) != 0) {
+	if ((route->flags & RTF_GATEWAY) != 0
+		&& (buffer->msg_flags & (MSG_BCAST | MSG_MCAST)) == 0) {
 		TRACE("  gateway route\n");
 
 		// This route involves a gateway, we need to use the gateway address
-		// instead of the destination address:
+		// instead of the destination address. Not for broadcasts and
+		// multicasts, though: they stay on the link (a multicast to a group
+		// without a route of its own takes the default route), and their
+		// link address comes from the destination address; the gateway's
+		// would give a multicast address nobody listens to.
 		if (route->gateway == NULL)
 			return B_MISMATCHED_VALUES;
 		memcpy(buffer->destination, route->gateway, route->gateway->sa_len);
